from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,html,zipfile
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent
records=json.loads((R/'scene.json').read_text())
parts=[r for r in records if not r['component']]
with (R/'PARTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf-8-sig') as f:
    w=csv.writer(f);w.writerow(['Assembly','Part','STL filename','File label','Physical marking','Notes'])
    for r in parts:w.writerow([r['role'],r['name'],r['file'],'Soham Basanwar',r['personalization'],r['notes']])

def pic(src,label):return f'<figure><img src="previews/{src}" loading="lazy" alt="{html.escape(label)}"><figcaption>{label}</figcaption></figure>'
body='''<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Dual-Reality Maze · Revision 07</title><style>
*{box-sizing:border-box}body{margin:0;background:#11151d;color:#e5e6eb;font:17px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:44px 24px}h1{font:42px Georgia;margin:8px 0;color:#e9c68f}h2{font:29px Georgia;color:#e9c68f;margin-top:48px}h3{font-size:21px}p{max-width:900px}a{color:#9ecbff}.eyebrow{letter-spacing:.15em;font-size:12px;color:#b3a087}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(320px,1fr));gap:20px}figure{margin:0;background:#1a212d;border-radius:14px;overflow:hidden}img{width:100%;display:block}figcaption{padding:13px 18px;font-size:14px;color:#c8cbd5}.card{background:#1a212d;padding:22px;border-radius:12px}button{background:#caa169;color:#141922;border:0;border-radius:8px;font:inherit;padding:10px 20px;cursor:pointer;margin:6px}table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:14px}td,th{text-align:left;padding:12px;border-bottom:1px solid #354050;vertical-align:top}.status{padding:15px;border-left:3px solid #caa169;background:#202431}details{margin:20px 0}summary{cursor:pointer}code{font-size:13px}
</style></head><body><main><div class="eyebrow">SOHAM BASANWAR · DESIGN REVIEW · 25 OCTOBER 2026</div><h1>Dual-Reality Maze</h1><p>Revision 07 · compact rune gate, softer battery access and personalized parts.</p><p class="status">Actual CAD renders. Prototype fit, printed latch strength, light transmission and powered operation remain unverified.</p>'''
body+=pic('family-charcoal.png','The three matching enclosures. Colour is illustrative; final structural filament is undecided.')
body+='''<h2>A gate that fits a handheld</h2><p>The motor is concealed inside the Architect. A rotating disk changes the arched window from bars to an open passage, with a nominal 110° sweep. The cover rises <strong>6.8 mm</strong> above the lid, compared with approximately 61 mm for the previous tower.</p><div class="grid"><div><figure><img id="gate" src="previews/gate-closed.png" alt="Compact gate closed"><figcaption id="gateCaption">Closed: bars across the window.</figcaption></figure><button onclick="setGate(false)">Closed</button><button onclick="setGate(true)">Open</button></div>'''
body+=pic('gate-mechanism.png','Cover removed: internal SG90 reference, removable cradle and disk. Supplied horn fits beneath the disk; its actual dimensions must be measured.')+'</div>'
body+='''<p>A clear PET viewing shield is recommended before handling the moving mechanism. The CAD review leaves the viewport open to expose the disk. Calibrate limits with the actual servo and fitted horn; the visual change is a physical gate-state indicator, not a functioning miniature passage.</p><details><summary>Other styles considered and design references</summary><table><tr><th>Style</th><th>Reason to choose it</th><th>Trade-off</th></tr><tr><td>Rotary rune window</td><td>Low silhouette and an actual open/closed arch</td><td>Fitted horn pocket and viewing shield</td></tr><tr><td>Lock-state pointer</td><td>Simplest motion and fewest parts</td><td>Less literal than a gate</td></tr><tr><td>Miniature drawbridge</td><td>Obvious opening movement</td><td>Projects up when raised</td></tr></table><p>Our own window layout, informed by the general servo/shutter approach in <a href="https://projecthub.arduino.cc/jkiiski/electronic-shutter-control-for-pinhole-camera-2f25e6">this creator’s SG90 shutter project</a>. <a href="https://towerpro.com.tw/product/sg90-analog/">TowerPro nominal dimensions</a> do not verify the user’s clone or horn.</p></details>'''
body+='<h2>Controller and Main views</h2><div class="grid">'
for role in ['explorer','architect','main']:body+=pic(role+'-assembled.png',role.title()+' · assembled')
body+='</div><h2>Battery access and internal layout</h2><p>The door has a rounded exposed perimeter and a broader rolled seating transition. Two leading tabs and a release catch retain it. The name sits on the inside of the door, away from the palm. Physical grip and latch coupons are still essential.</p><div class="grid">'
for role in ['explorer','architect']:body+=pic(role+'-battery-door.png',role.title()+' · underside access')
for role in ['explorer','architect','main']:body+=pic(role+'-internal.png',role.title()+' · base, component reservations and provisional ESP32 space')
body+='</div><h2>Your name and initials</h2><p>Large parts carry “Soham Basanwar”; selected small parts carry “SB”. Thin keepers and tiny fit-sensitive parts remain unmarked. Every printed part is labelled with your full name in its filename, CAD object label and <a href="PARTS.csv">parts list</a>.</p>'
body+=pic('personalization.png','Actual engraved parts: battery-door interior and selected SB markings. These are geometry, not a texture overlay.')
body+='<details><summary>All printed parts and their marking</summary><table><tr><th>Assembly / part</th><th>Marking</th><th>File</th></tr>'
for r in parts:body+=f'<tr><td>{r["role"].title()} / {r["name"].replace("_"," ")}</td><td>{html.escape(r["personalization"])}</td><td><a href="prototype-stl/{r["file"]}">STL</a></td></tr>'
body+='</table></details><h2>Review and files</h2><p><a href="README.md">Design and mechanism notes</a> · <a href="PRINT_AND_ASSEMBLY.md">Print and assembly guidance</a> · <a href="DIMENSION_CHECKLIST.csv">Measurement checklist</a> · <a href="REVIEW_VALIDATION.json">Validation report</a> · <a href="../revision-06/index.html">Previous revision</a></p><div class="grid">'
for role in ['explorer','architect','main']:body+=f'<div class="card"><h3>{role.title()}</h3><a href="cad/{role}-revision07.FCStd">FreeCAD assembly</a><br><a href="cad/{role}-printed-parts.step">STEP solids</a></div>'
body+='</div><p>Open a native assembly in FreeCAD, use the parts list to select files, and test the fit coupons in PrusaSlicer before committing to full shells. No extra software or machine-specific G-code is required.</p></main><script>function setGate(open){document.getElementById("gate").src="previews/gate-"+(open?"open":"closed")+".png";document.getElementById("gateCaption").textContent=open?"Open: the clear arch sector aligns with the viewport.":"Closed: bars across the window."}</script></body></html>'
(R/'index.html').write_text(body,encoding='utf-8')
(R/'Open_Revision07.FCMacro').write_text("from pathlib import Path\nimport FreeCAD as App\nR=Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nfor role in ['explorer','architect','main']:\n    doc=App.openDocument(str(R/'cad'/(role+'-revision07.FCStd')))\n    for o in doc.getObject('ComponentEnvelopes').Group:o.ViewObject.Visibility=False\n    Gui.activeDocument().activeView().viewAxonometric()\n    Gui.activeDocument().activeView().fitAll()\n",encoding='utf-8')
print('Review gallery and parts list written')
